     {
      "text": "48-year-old male presenting with excessive thirst and frequent urination for 5 weeks. Character: passing urine many times, also at night; radiation: n/a; aggravated by sweet food; relieved by nothing. Severity 2/10. Associated: tiredness, weight loss. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 2 years. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg. Allergy: peanuts. Family: no similar illness. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
